  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Polar stratospheric clouds&nbsp;surface act on catalyst&nbsp;which provided surface on which hydrolysis of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ClONO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> takes place to form&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HOCl</mi></math> (Hypochlorous acid)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ClONO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>HOCl</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Polar stratospheric clouds (PSCs) play a central role in the formation of&nbsp;the ozone hole&nbsp;in the Antarctic and Arctic.</p>"
